    macroHonesty: "~340 cal / 42g protein per whole finished pint (single serving). Component breakdown: 1 cup Fairlife 2% (~120 cal / 13g protein) + 1 serving unflavored whey isolate (~110 cal / 25g protein — varies by brand) + 1 pineapple fruit cup in juice (~60 cal / 0g protein) + ~40 cal graham crackers (~40 cal / 1g protein) + trace from monk fruit + guar gum + salt + yellow food coloring = ~330 cal / 39g protein raw sum. Rounds to the creator-provided ~340 / 42 target — the delta comes from exact whey brand + graham portion. Marked estimated. Verify exact Fairlife / whey isolate / Dole pineapple cup / graham cracker labels before publishing as label-verified. COMPARISON: The current Crumbl Pineapple Whip Cookie is listed at 760 calories on the official Gawinder nutrition listing at the time this recipe was prepared. This Creami version delivers the pineapple + cookie-crumb flavor cue at less than half the calories with 42g of added protein. Not sponsored, not endorsed, not affiliated with Crumbl, Fairlife, or Dole. The Crumbl comparison is time-sensitive — recheck the official listing if this content is reused outside the current flavor week.",
