    useThisWhen: "You want a red velvet protein dessert with fudgy brownie pockets and a cream-frosting-adjacent white-chocolate drizzle finish, inspired by the Crumbl Red Velvet Cookie Thins (Set of 2) — as a whole-pint Creami with the macros a red velvet cookie doesn't offer. Ep. 9 of CrumblCreamiCut and the FINALE of Week 3 — closes the chocolate-adjacent Week 3 trilogy (Mallow W3F1 chocolate + Dubai W3F2 chocolate-pistachio + Red Velvet W3F3 chocolate-cream-cheese). This ep is a SYNTHESIS rather than a series-first: it stacks (a) protein-brownie Respin mix-in — the technique that made W3F1 Mallow work, (b) flavor emulsion in the pre-freeze base — introduced in W3F2 Dubai, (c) a NEW post-scoop white-chocolate drizzle finish, the first CCC ep to melt white chocolate as a drizzle carrier. Half the Dutch-cocoa charge (1/2 tbsp vs 1 tbsp in Mallow/Dubai) — the base is intentionally lighter so the red velvet emulsion + white-chocolate drizzle carry the identity, not the cocoa. Ties Mallow's 48g protein pint as the highest-protein CCC ep so far.",
    priorEpisode: "/cookbook/dubai-style-chocolate-thin-sandwich-cookie-creami",
    flavorTarget: "First spoon: subtle cocoa + red velvet emulsion note across the base — reads chocolate-adjacent, not straight chocolate. Bite: fudgy red velvet protein-brownie pieces distributed through the Respin land as cookie-crumb pockets. Top: warm white-chocolate drizzle over the scoops delivers the cream-cheese-frosting cue that separates red velvet from plain chocolate. Whole pint should taste like the Crumbl Red Velvet Cookie Thins deconstructed into ice cream — light cocoa + emulsion base + brownie pockets + white-chocolate drizzle, one bowl.",
