    macroHonesty: "~370 cal / 48g protein per whole finished pint (single serving). Component breakdown: 1 cup Fairlife 2% (~120 cal / 13g protein) + 1 serving unflavored whey isolate (~110 cal / 25g protein — varies by brand) + 2 tbsp monk fruit sweetener (~0 cal) + 1/8 tsp guar gum (~trace) + 1/2 tbsp Dutch cocoa (~10 cal / trace protein — HALF the Mallow/Dubai charge) + 1 tsp red velvet emulsion (~5 cal / 0g protein) + 1/3 red velvet protein brownie (~75 cal / 8g protein — the protein bump that ties Mallow's 48g headline, verify current label) + 1 tbsp white chocolate chips (~55 cal / trace protein — varies by brand) + 1 tbsp Fairlife fat-free milk (~5 cal / 1g protein) = ~380 cal / 47g protein raw sum. Rounds to the creator-provided ~370 / 48 target. Marked estimated. Verify exact Fairlife / whey isolate / Dutch cocoa / red velvet emulsion / red velvet protein brownie / white chocolate labels before publishing as label-verified. Compared to Crumbl Red Velvet Cookie Thins (Set of 2) as the reference flavor — the Creami version delivers similar flavor identity with high protein density (48g whole pint) vs the sugar-heavy cookie set. Not sponsored, not endorsed, not affiliated with Crumbl, LorAnn, Ninja, Fairlife, or any red-velvet-protein-brownie / white-chocolate brand. Allergens: dairy (milk + whey isolate) + egg (protein brownie) + wheat (protein brownie) + soy (protein brownie / white chocolate lecithin). NO TREE NUTS in this ep (unlike W3F2 Dubai which had pistachio) — verify labels before claiming free-of.",
