      framing: "CrumblCreamiCut Week 3's third flavor and the WEEK 3 FINALE — closes the chocolate-adjacent Week 3 trilogy (Mallow W3F1 chocolate-marshmallow + Dubai W3F2 chocolate-pistachio + Red Velvet W3F3 chocolate-cream-cheese). Ep. 9 is a SYNTHESIS ep, not a series-first introduction — it stacks (a) protein-brownie Respin mix-in from W3F1 Mallow, (b) flavor emulsion in the pre-freeze base from W3F2 Dubai, and (c) a NEW post-scoop white-chocolate drizzle finish (first CCC ep to melt white chocolate as a drizzle carrier — earlier drizzle finishes were marshmallow creme W3F1, graham crumb W2F3 Key Lime, or pistachio-cream-coated kataifi W3F2 Dubai). Half the Dutch-cocoa charge (1/2 tbsp vs the 1 tbsp used in W3F1/W3F2) — the base is intentionally lighter here so the emulsion + drizzle carry the red velvet identity. Ties Mallow's 48g protein pint as the highest-protein CCC ep so far. Uses a different milk-fat level for the drizzle (Fairlife fat-free) than the base (Fairlife 2%) — the ONLY CCC ep that requires two milk-fat levels. Red velvet identity question is deliberately unresolved in the recipe copy — the caption asks 'is red velvet chocolate, or its own flavor?' for engagement; the recipe body treats it as chocolate-adjacent-with-emulsion-identity rather than picking a side. Reference flavor: Crumbl Red Velvet Cookie Thins (Set of 2) — recheck the flavor cycle if content is reused after the current cycle.",
