      priorEpisode: "/cookbook/red-velvet-cookie-thins-creami",
      framing: "CrumblCreamiCut Week 4's first flavor — a fresh weekly start after Week 3's cocoa-forward trilogy (Mallow W3F1 → Dubai W3F2 → Red Velvet W3F3). Two series-firsts: (1) POWDERED PEANUT BUTTER in the base — no prior CCC episode used PB2/PBfit in the pre-freeze base, and it's what unlocks the peanut-butter-cookie identity vs simply adding peanut butter as a topping; (2) PROTEIN BAR as the Respin mix-in AND post-scoop topping — every prior CCC used a protein BROWNIE for the Respin (Prime Bites Cookie Monster in W3F1 Mallow, red velvet brownie in W3F3, etc.); this ep swaps to a peanut-caramel PROTEIN BAR (Barebells Salty Peanut Caramel filmed) so the mix-in supplies pre-formed caramel/chocolate/peanut chunks instead of fudgy brownie pockets. HIGHEST-PROTEIN CCC ep so far — 53g whole pint vs the 47-48g range across Ep. 7-9. The 5g bump stacks the powdered PB (+~5g protein) and the peanut-caramel protein bar (~10g protein per 1/2 bar, vs ~8g for the brownie halves in Ep. 7-9). Same 1 cup Fairlife + whey + guar gum + salt foundation as the whole series. Bar goes in via Respin (same cycle family as W2F2 Beach Bum / W2F3 Key Lime / W3F1 Mallow). Reference flavor: Crumbl SNICKERS Peanut Butter Cookie — recheck the flavor cycle if content is reused after the current cycle. Not sponsored by Crumbl, SNICKERS, or Barebells.",
