      kid: "SAFETY: Whole petite pickles + firm cheese cubes are texture-appropriate for most kids but under 4s should have pickles sliced lengthwise (not left whole) and cheese cubed small (1/2-inch or less). Pretzel crisps are flat and thin — lower choking risk than round hard pretzels, but still watch for kids who don't chew thoroughly. Per CDC + AAP choking-prevention guidance. Kids can help place components — turns snack prep into low-pressure participation. Not school-safe by default: some schools restrict pretzel wheat/gluten; check the school's allergen and formulation rules before packing outside the home.",
