    macroHonesty: "About 280 cal / 16g protein per snack box — user-approved headline, not label-verified. Broad component approximation: 1 large hard-boiled egg (~70 cal / 6g protein) + 1 portion (~60 cal) dried strawberries (~0.5g protein) + 1 Laughing Cow-style light wedge (~35-50 cal / 2-3g protein) + 0.75 oz salted peanuts (~120 cal / 5g protein) ≈ 285-300 cal / 13.5-15g protein raw sum. Rounds to the ~280 / 16 published headline with wedge + peanut brand variation. Verify against your exact labels before publishing as macro-accurate. Ep. 9's snack-box macro ratio (1:17.5 protein-to-cal) is consistent with the series average (Ep. 5 Mediterranean = 1:16.9, Ep. 8 Deli Dill = 1:12.5); snack boxes optimize for kid-familiar + protein-density-vs-typical-snacks, not the 1:10 Powerups line. Not sponsored, not endorsed, not affiliated with Laughing Cow or any specific egg / dried fruit / cheese / peanut brand.",
